zig-out/
.zig-cache/

# A write stages the new log in a temp file alongside it and renames it into
# place (D11). The tool removes it on every path it controls, but it cannot
# clean up after a SIGKILL — and the log lives in a source-controlled
# directory, so an abandoned one is otherwise a `git add -A` away from being
# committed. Pattern matches src/log.zig's `.<basename>.tmp-<hex>`.
.*.tmp-*
